{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{35}{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{35}{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 7\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{35}{4} & =\\frac{7}{4}b \\\\ b & =\\frac{\\frac{35}{4}}{\\frac{7}{4}} \\\\ b & =5\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=5\\,\\text{cm}.$" 13194139536010 17592186045443 true] [17592186556367 1068 #edb/ref 17592186556388 13194139536010 17592186045443 true] [17592186556367 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139536010 17592186045443 true] [17592186556367 1071 "![](images/76/76bdcef8f267043fe1f9c97f989ff3d6bfdf3b071158501cf43aef78976e93eb.png)\n\nThe area of the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{1247\\sqrt{2}}{64}\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.$ Then, $AC=${{field-1}} $\\text{cm}.$" 13194139536010 17592186045443 true] [17592186556367 1072 #uuid "3adcb0ec-bc29-5a54-9e87-f2d6aa44e246" 13194139536010 17592186045443 true] [17592186556367 1074 "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=\\frac{43}{4}\\text{ cm} \\\\ b & =AC \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{1247\\sqrt{2}}{64} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot \\frac{43}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{1247\\sqrt{2}}{64} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot \\frac{43}{4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1247\\sqrt{2}}{64} & =\\frac{43\\sqrt{2}}{16}b \\\\ b & =\\frac{\\frac{1247\\sqrt{2}}{64}}{\\frac{43\\sqrt{2}}{16}} \\\\ b & =\\frac{29}{4}\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=\\frac{29}{4}\\,\\text{cm}.$" 1319413953601